1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,390
Okay, tumor progression.

2
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:05,410
Once you've understood the idea of carcinogenesis

3
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:07,850
and you understand that carcinogenesis

4
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:11,390
is going to knock out key important regulatory elements,

5
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:16,530
then the next notion is that as a tumor cell grows

6
00:00:16,530 --> 00:00:19,510
and begins to produce additional daughter cells,

7
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:21,470
it will pick up additional mutations.

8
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:23,330
And those additional mutations

9
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,810
will allow for tumor progression.

10
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:28,170
And so eventually what will happen in the case of cancer

11
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,550
is that accumulation of mutations

12
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,990
will result in invasion and spread.

13
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:36,170
And remember that the hallmark of cancer,

14
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:38,170
of malignant neoplasia,

15
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:40,490
is that it locally invades

16
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:44,410
and the defining feature of malignant neoplasia or cancer

17
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:47,750
is that it will spread to distant sites,

18
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:49,750
which is also called metastasis.

19
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:52,770
Now in order for this spread to occur,

20
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:54,910
there are a few characteristic changes

21
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:56,930
that have to arise within the tumor

22
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,330
to promote such spread.

23
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:03,370
And so what I'd like to do is walk you through those.

24
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:06,490
The first is downregulation of E-cadherin.

25
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:09,370
Normally, when you look at epithelial cells,

26
00:01:09,490 --> 00:01:10,990
these are epithelial cells,

27
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:13,450
you're well aware from histology

28
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:16,230
that epithelial cells sit on a basement membrane

29
00:01:16,230 --> 00:01:18,310
and that these epithelial cells

30
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:22,810
are attached to each other by various molecules,

31
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:26,090
one subgroup of which is called the cadherins.

32
00:01:26,570 --> 00:01:27,750
And within cadherin,

33
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:30,030
a particular molecule is e-cadherin.

34
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:31,690
Now, cadherins,

35
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:34,010
they keep the cells attached to one another.

36
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:37,190
And if tumor is going to form,

37
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:38,850
for example, from this cell,

38
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:41,390
what needs to happen in order for it

39
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:43,150
to be able to spread locally

40
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,750
and then to metastasize

41
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,870
is this tumor cell needs to be able

42
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:48,970
to dissociate from its neighbors.

43
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:51,470
One way by which it dissociates from its neighbors

44
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:56,450
is via a downregulation of E-cadherin.

45
00:01:57,410 --> 00:01:59,290
And so one characteristic that I've listed here

46
00:01:59,290 --> 00:02:02,290
in your text is downregulation of E-cadherin.

47
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:06,070
Now, once E-cadherin is downregulated,

48
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:11,970
then this cell will attach to the laminin,

49
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:15,250
which is present in association

50
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:16,470
with the basement membrane.

51
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:19,550
Go back and recall from normal histology

52
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:21,090
that the basement membrane

53
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:25,210
is basically composed of two key molecules.

54
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:27,090
The first is collagen IV.

55
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:29,070
Collagen IV makes up the vast majority

56
00:02:29,070 --> 00:02:29,990
of the basement membrane.

57
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:31,350
And then the basement membrane

58
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:33,630
also has laminin associated with it.

59
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:34,810
And so the cells,

60
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:38,410
once they dissociate from the neighboring cells,

61
00:02:38,690 --> 00:02:41,110
will actually attach to the laminin

62
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:42,210
within the basement membrane.

63
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:44,110
Now, once they attach to the laminin

64
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:45,190
within the basement membrane,

65
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:46,310
the next step would be

66
00:02:46,310 --> 00:02:47,810
to destroy the basement membrane.

67
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:49,770
And tumor cells can eventually develop

68
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:52,430
the ability to produce collagenase,

69
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:53,790
in particular collagenase

70
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,590
that would destroy collagen type IV.

71
00:02:55,950 --> 00:02:57,170
Binding to the laminin

72
00:02:57,170 --> 00:02:58,990
and destruction of the basement membrane

73
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:00,390
will then allow this cell

74
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:02,030
to eventually come out here

75
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:03,770
into the extracellular matrix.

76
00:03:03,770 --> 00:03:05,710
Now, once the cell

77
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:07,210
is within the extracellular matrix,

78
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:09,510
it will attach itself to fibronectin.

79
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:12,110
It'll attach itself to fibronectin

80
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:13,670
within the extracellular matrix,

81
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:15,270
and then it can spread locally.

82
00:03:15,770 --> 00:03:17,170
Eventually, it'll gain access

83
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:18,570
to either the blood vessel,

84
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:21,490
or it may gain access to lymphatics.

85
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:23,590
And when it gains access to lymphatics,

86
00:03:23,650 --> 00:03:24,770
it'll spread to lymph node.

87
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:26,910
And if it gains access to blood vessel,

88
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:28,710
it will spread to distant sites.

89
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:30,250
And so this is sort of a little bit

90
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,190
of a paradigm, step number one,

91
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:33,770
down-regulation of e-cadherin.

92
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:35,190
Step number two,

93
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:37,170
the cells then attach to laminin.

94
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:38,930
Step number three,

95
00:03:39,110 --> 00:03:40,510
they destroy the basement membrane

96
00:03:40,510 --> 00:03:42,050
using collagenase type IV.

97
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:43,430
Step number four,

98
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:44,870
they attach to fibronectin

99
00:03:44,870 --> 00:03:46,190
in the extracellular matrix

100
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:47,570
and begin to spread locally.

101
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,150
And then step number five

102
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:50,930
would be to enter into the vascular

103
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:52,130
or lymphatic space.

104
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:54,390
And if we go back to the slide,

105
00:03:54,830 --> 00:03:56,830
each of these steps is listed here

106
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:58,830
in sequence,

107
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:00,150
and you can review this

108
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:01,130
within your text as well.

109
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,510
I've already basically explained

110
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:03,510
this slide to you.

111
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:06,570
Recall that one of the hallmarks

112
00:04:06,570 --> 00:04:07,730
or the key hallmark

113
00:04:07,730 --> 00:04:09,250
of a malignant tumor,

114
00:04:09,430 --> 00:04:10,110
i.e. cancer,

115
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:12,530
is that it will spread to distant sites.

116
00:04:13,150 --> 00:04:15,470
And so it's important to know

117
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:16,790
that carcinomas,

118
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:19,950
they tend to spread via the lymphatics.

119
00:04:20,710 --> 00:04:23,030
So the place where you expect

120
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:24,210
to see carcinoma

121
00:04:24,210 --> 00:04:26,830
would be the regional draining lymph nodes.

122
00:04:27,190 --> 00:04:28,310
I'll just give you one example.

123
00:04:28,490 --> 00:04:30,150
Take, for example, breast cancer.

124
00:04:30,590 --> 00:04:32,550
So when a patient develops breast cancer,

125
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:35,050
one of the common sites

126
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:37,210
or one of the initial sites of spread

127
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:38,790
is into the lymphatics

128
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:40,430
and then through the lymphatics

129
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:42,010
into the axillary lymph nodes.

130
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:43,890
And recall that the axillary lymph nodes

131
00:04:43,890 --> 00:04:44,890
are the lymph nodes

132
00:04:44,890 --> 00:04:46,090
that drain the breast.

133
00:04:46,710 --> 00:04:48,710
And so one important principle

134
00:04:48,710 --> 00:04:51,170
to know about cancer

135
00:04:51,170 --> 00:04:53,750
is that carcinoma spread

136
00:04:53,750 --> 00:04:56,250
via lymphatics to regional nodes.

137
00:04:56,390 --> 00:04:57,190
General principle.

138
00:04:57,830 --> 00:04:58,850
Carcinoma spread

139
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:00,210
via lymphatics

140
00:05:00,210 --> 00:05:01,430
to regional lymph nodes.

141
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:02,650
To highlight this,

142
00:05:02,730 --> 00:05:04,450
I've placed a picture in your text.

143
00:05:04,890 --> 00:05:06,070
And you can clearly see

144
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:06,490
what I've,

145
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:07,870
this picture basically

146
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,030
is that of a lymph node.

147
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:10,190
So I'm highlighting here

148
00:05:10,190 --> 00:05:11,570
the capsule of the lymph node.

149
00:05:12,090 --> 00:05:13,250
This area here

150
00:05:13,250 --> 00:05:14,830
represents the normal lymph node

151
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:16,290
with these small dark blue cells.

152
00:05:16,610 --> 00:05:17,250
And then clearly,

153
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:17,870
we can see

154
00:05:17,870 --> 00:05:19,870
that there is some tumor here

155
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:21,490
which is replacing the lymph node.

156
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:22,390
And notice that the tumor

157
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:23,210
has a bunch of

158
00:05:23,210 --> 00:05:25,030
white spaces within it.

159
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:25,930
And these are glands.

160
00:05:26,090 --> 00:05:28,430
And this is an adenocarcinoma.

161
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:30,230
And so I've only placed this here

162
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:30,990
to remind you

163
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:32,730
of the general principle

164
00:05:32,730 --> 00:05:34,950
that carcinomas

165
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:35,950
tend to spread

166
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:36,990
via the lymphatics

167
00:05:36,990 --> 00:05:38,350
into regional lymph nodes.

168
00:05:39,030 --> 00:05:40,430
Cancer can also spread

169
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:41,490
hematogenously.

170
00:05:42,150 --> 00:05:43,410
And hematogenous spread

171
00:05:43,410 --> 00:05:45,390
is characteristic of sarcomas.

172
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:46,570
Recall from the beginning

173
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:47,290
of this lecture

174
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:49,130
that sarcomas are

175
00:05:49,130 --> 00:05:50,850
a malignancy

176
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,410
of mesenchymal tissue.

177
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:53,350
So for example,

178
00:05:53,470 --> 00:05:54,790
an osteosarcoma

179
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:57,090
is a malignant bone tumor.

180
00:05:57,470 --> 00:05:58,550
A chondrosarcoma

181
00:05:58,550 --> 00:05:59,930
is a malignant cartilage tumor.

182
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:01,510
A liposarcoma

183
00:06:01,510 --> 00:06:03,430
is a malignant tumor

184
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:04,510
of adipose tissue.

185
00:06:04,890 --> 00:06:05,950
So mesenchymal

186
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:07,170
or connective tissues

187
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:08,570
when they're malignant,

188
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:09,690
we call them sarcomas.

189
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:11,030
And sarcomas

190
00:06:11,030 --> 00:06:11,810
tend to spread

191
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:12,610
through the blood.

192
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:13,890
They go into the blood vessels

193
00:06:13,890 --> 00:06:14,890
and then they spread

194
00:06:14,890 --> 00:06:15,790
to distant sites.

195
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:17,510
So that's a general principle.

196
00:06:17,670 --> 00:06:18,550
So principle A

197
00:06:18,550 --> 00:06:19,790
of this discussion,

198
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:20,610
principle A

199
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:21,850
is that carcinomas

200
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:22,930
go into the lymphatics

201
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:23,370
and spread

202
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:24,610
to the regional lymph nodes.

203
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:25,890
And principle B

204
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:27,010
would be that sarcomas

205
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:27,870
go into the blood

206
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:29,210
and a characteristic

207
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:29,870
site of spread

208
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:30,550
would be the lungs.

209
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:31,530
Now,

210
00:06:31,650 --> 00:06:33,090
there are some exceptions

211
00:06:33,090 --> 00:06:34,190
and so the exceptions

212
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:35,130
become high yield

213
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:35,890
because they make

214
00:06:35,890 --> 00:06:37,230
for nice test material.

215
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:38,590
There are a subset

216
00:06:38,590 --> 00:06:39,490
of carcinomas

217
00:06:39,490 --> 00:06:41,010
that like to spread

218
00:06:41,010 --> 00:06:42,250
into the blood.

219
00:06:42,250 --> 00:06:43,090
And so again,

220
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:44,150
they're breaking the rule.

221
00:06:44,650 --> 00:06:45,370
And so it's important

222
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,050
to be familiar

223
00:06:46,050 --> 00:06:47,370
with these exceptions

224
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:48,450
because again,

225
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:49,810
it makes for nice

226
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:50,430
test material.

227
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:52,310
So one exception

228
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:53,950
is renal cell carcinoma.

229
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:55,450
And renal cell carcinoma,

230
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:57,590
it's one of the characteristics

231
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:58,690
of renal cell carcinoma

232
00:06:58,690 --> 00:06:59,550
is that it likes

233
00:06:59,550 --> 00:06:59,970
to invade

234
00:06:59,970 --> 00:07:00,810
into the renal vein.

235
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:01,890
And when it invades

236
00:07:01,890 --> 00:07:02,750
into the renal vein,

237
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:04,190
it can present

238
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:05,450
with distant metastases.

239
00:07:05,590 --> 00:07:06,510
And it's not uncommon

240
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:07,150
for a patient

241
00:07:07,150 --> 00:07:08,370
with renal cell carcinoma

242
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:09,150
to present

243
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:10,290
with distant metastases.

244
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:12,990
Another carcinoma

245
00:07:12,990 --> 00:07:14,490
that likes to go into,

246
00:07:15,090 --> 00:07:15,890
that likes to spread

247
00:07:15,890 --> 00:07:16,710
hematogenously

248
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,630
is hepatocellular carcinoma.

249
00:07:19,190 --> 00:07:20,210
This likes to invade

250
00:07:20,210 --> 00:07:20,990
the hepatic vein

251
00:07:20,990 --> 00:07:21,950
and then can spread

252
00:07:21,950 --> 00:07:23,110
to distant sites.

253
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:25,470
A third carcinoma

254
00:07:25,470 --> 00:07:27,030
that likes to spread

255
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:27,890
hematogenously

256
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:29,650
is follicular carcinoma

257
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:30,390
of the thyroid.

258
00:07:31,150 --> 00:07:31,850
And the fourth

259
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:32,970
is choriocarcinoma.

260
00:07:33,030 --> 00:07:33,790
And choriocarcinoma

261
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:35,170
is really easy to remember

262
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:36,870
because what is

263
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:37,810
choriocarcinoma?

264
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:38,730
Choriocarcinoma

265
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:39,550
is a malignancy

266
00:07:39,550 --> 00:07:40,610
of placental tissue.

267
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:41,310
In particular,

268
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:42,750
the cells that line

269
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:44,790
the villi of the placenta.

270
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:45,930
And those cells

271
00:07:45,930 --> 00:07:47,230
are called trophoblasts.

272
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:48,530
And so choriocarcinoma

273
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:49,390
is a malignancy

274
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:50,250
of trophoblasts.

275
00:07:50,430 --> 00:07:51,470
And guess what trophoblasts

276
00:07:51,470 --> 00:07:52,230
are designed to do

277
00:07:52,230 --> 00:07:52,870
by their nature?

278
00:07:53,090 --> 00:07:53,610
They're designed

279
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:54,890
to find a blood vessel

280
00:07:54,890 --> 00:07:56,170
and invade into blood vessel.

281
00:07:56,490 --> 00:07:56,810
In fact,

282
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:57,410
that's the job

283
00:07:57,410 --> 00:07:58,030
of the placenta.

284
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:00,450
And so choriocarcinoma,

285
00:08:00,930 --> 00:08:01,570
I don't think

286
00:08:01,570 --> 00:08:02,190
it's too hard

287
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:02,790
to remember

288
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:03,830
that it's going

289
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:04,850
to go into the blood

290
00:08:04,850 --> 00:08:05,370
and it's going

291
00:08:05,370 --> 00:08:07,190
to spread hematogenously

292
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:08,050
because that's sort

293
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:08,850
of what those cells

294
00:08:08,850 --> 00:08:09,870
are programmed to do

295
00:08:09,870 --> 00:08:10,690
to begin with.

296
00:08:11,410 --> 00:08:12,370
Now a third way

297
00:08:12,370 --> 00:08:13,270
by which cancer

298
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:14,690
can spread

299
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:16,390
is by seeding

300
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:17,610
body cavities.

301
00:08:18,010 --> 00:08:19,110
And that's characteristic

302
00:08:19,110 --> 00:08:20,670
of ovarian carcinoma.

303
00:08:21,110 --> 00:08:22,030
Ovarian carcinoma

304
00:08:22,030 --> 00:08:23,790
has the propensity

305
00:08:23,790 --> 00:08:25,430
to seed body cavities.

306
00:08:25,930 --> 00:08:27,210
It often involves

307
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:28,850
the omentum

308
00:08:28,850 --> 00:08:29,670
of the abdomen.

309
00:08:30,130 --> 00:08:31,370
And so a classic picture

310
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:32,050
that can arise

311
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:33,170
is something like this

312
00:08:33,170 --> 00:08:35,410
where we can clearly see

313
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:36,270
that we're in the abdomen.

314
00:08:36,450 --> 00:08:37,870
This is a loop of bowel.

315
00:08:38,170 --> 00:08:39,310
And this is cancer

316
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,410
that has completely

317
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:42,290
replaced the omentum.

318
00:08:43,470 --> 00:08:44,830
Were we to actually

319
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:45,610
cut through this,

320
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:46,690
this would be very thick.

321
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:47,650
And when you cut

322
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:48,730
through this with a knife,

323
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:49,730
it sort of has

324
00:08:49,730 --> 00:08:51,270
the consistency of cake.

325
00:08:51,830 --> 00:08:53,530
And so another term

326
00:08:53,530 --> 00:08:55,650
to describe this phenomena

327
00:08:55,650 --> 00:08:57,550
is called omental caking.

328
00:08:58,150 --> 00:08:59,870
And that is an important term

329
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:00,710
to be familiar with

330
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:01,790
and I've placed it

331
00:09:01,790 --> 00:09:02,930
in your text as well.

332
00:09:02,930 --> 00:09:05,110
So that concludes

333
00:09:05,110 --> 00:09:06,370
this section

334
00:09:06,370 --> 00:09:07,690
on tumor progression.

